{
 "summary": "Checkout failures (gateway 502s, up to 71.8% error ratio) are a timeout cascade from inventory POST /reserve, which became slow (p95 up to 4.77s) right after inventory was deployed 3.1.5 -> 3.2.1 at 07:18:17Z. Orders returns 504 when its call to inventory exceeds its timeout, and the gateway relays that as 502. Inventory itself returns no 5xx; it is slow, not failing. Rolling back inventory to 3.1.5 is the most direct mitigation.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "The inventory 3.2.1 release, deployed at 07:18:17Z, made POST /reserve slow (self time about 2.4-2.6s, p95 up to 4.77s). Orders' calls to inventory time out, so orders returns 504 and the gateway returns 502 on POST /checkout. The deploy is linked to the symptoms by timing (latency onset 15-30s later) and by traces putting the dominant self time in inventory POST /reserve on release 3.2.1. No logs are available to confirm the code-level mechanism.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-190058c637be",
   "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
   "ev-51525d7035d0",
   "ev-1da116a62fee",
   "ev-c000e6b4f684"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders' timeout toward inventory (about 2s, judging by trace durations of 2.01-2.24s) is shorter than inventory's degraded latency. As a result, slow inventory responses become 504s rather than slow successes.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
    "ev-51525d7035d0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders' error ratio climbed to 100% by the end of the window, so checkouts eventually failed almost entirely.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-1da116a62fee"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:17Z",
   "event": "inventory deployed 3.1.5 -> 3.2.1 by ci-pipeline",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-190058c637be"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:32Z",
   "event": "orders 5xx ratio crosses 5% and p95 latency crosses 1s",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-1da116a62fee"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:47Z",
   "event": "inventory p95 latency crosses 1s (0% 5xx); gateway 5xx ratio and p95 latency cross thresholds",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-51525d7035d0",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:20:33Z",
   "event": "Sampled traces show gateway 502 <- orders 504, with dominant self time in inventory POST /reserve on 3.2.1 (first seen 07:20:33Z, last seen 07:20:43Z)",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "Gateway as origin: it only relays orders' 504 as a 502, and the dominant self time is not in the gateway.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders as origin: orders' 504s follow inventory's slowness, and the most self time is in inventory POST /reserve.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
    "ev-1da116a62fee"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Inventory returning errors: inventory's 5xx ratio is 0%, so the failure mode is latency, not inventory errors.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-51525d7035d0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "A traffic surge: request rates stay modest (gateway about 2.1 req/s on average, 2.46 at most).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "Logs could not be queried (backend timeout), so inventory 3.2.1 errors, slow-query or lock messages, and orders timeout messages are unverified.",
  "It is unclear what change in inventory 3.2.1 slows POST /reserve, for example a new downstream dependency, a DB query, or locking. No dependency metrics beneath inventory were collected.",
  "Orders' latency onset (07:18:32Z) is 15s earlier than inventory's p95 onset; this is likely a step/percentile artifact but is not confirmed.",
  "Traces cover only 07:20:33-07:20:43Z (20 samples); the earlier part of the incident is not represented in trace evidence."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Roll back inventory from 3.2.1 to 3.1.5.",
   "rationale": "The slowdown began right after this deploy, and traces attribute the dominant self time to inventory 3.2.1 POST /reserve.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-190058c637be",
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "After the rollback, confirm that inventory p95 latency and the orders and gateway 5xx ratios return to baseline.",
   "rationale": "This validates the causal link, which currently rests on timing and trace self time.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-51525d7035d0",
    "ev-1da116a62fee",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Re-run the log query for inventory and orders over 07:16-07:21Z.",
   "rationale": "Logs were unavailable and are needed to identify the mechanism behind the 3.2.1 slowdown.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "src-logs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Inspect example traces e1af7fdd63c588af3940a164158d28c1 and efc519b65a223a76d1b5de89ca1498b3, and diff inventory 3.1.5..3.2.1 for changes to the POST /reserve path.",
   "rationale": "This would pinpoint where inside /reserve the time is spent.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
    "ev-190058c637be"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
